---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
---

<Marketing
	title="Features · Obzly"
	description="Logs, traces, metrics, synthetic monitoring, infrastructure and cloud inventory, dashboards, alerts, MCP and enterprise features in the open source Obzly image."
	current="features"
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">Features</div>
			<h1>What Obzly does</h1>
			<p class="lede">Every feature on this page is in the open source image. Nothing here needs a licence key.</p>
			<nav class="jump" aria-label="Feature sections">
				<a href="#logs">Logs</a><a href="#traces">Traces</a><a href="#metrics">Metrics</a>
				<a href="#synthetics">Synthetics</a><a href="#infrastructure">Infrastructure</a>
				<a href="#dashboards">Dashboards &amp; Alerts</a><a href="#ai">AI observability &amp; MCP</a><a href="#enterprise">Enterprise</a>
			</nav>
		</div>

		<article class="feat" id="logs">
			<div class="txt">
				<div class="eyebrow">Logs</div>
				<h2>Search a week of logs in seconds</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><b>Search</b> by text and field, with a query builder or SQL and a field sidebar.</li>
					<li><b>Live tail</b> with cursor paging, so new arrivals don't shift the page you're reading.</li>
					<li><b>Patterns and anomalies</b>: new, spiking and dropping patterns against an earlier period.</li>
					<li><b>Log context</b>: the logs before and after any result, from the same pod or service.</li>
					<li><b>Promoted fields</b>: up to 12 per project become typed columns for fast filters and number ranges.</li>
					<li><b>Wide searches</b> read newest-first and stop once the page is full. Searching for an ID skips every segment whose bloom filter lacks it.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="specimen">
				<div class="lbl">Search bar</div>
				<pre><span class="k">level</span>:error <span class="k">service_name</span>:checkout <span class="s">"timeout"</span></pre>
