		<article class="feat" id="synthetics">
			<div class="txt">
				<div class="eyebrow">Synthetics</div>
				<h2>Know an endpoint is down before your users do</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><b>Checks</b>: HTTP with assertions on status, latency, headers and JSON; TLS certificates (expiry, chain, protocol, self-signed allowed per monitor); TCP; DNS; ICMP.</li>
					<li><b>Your own locations</b>: <code>obzly-probe</code> runs as a Linux service, a container or a Helm release, inside your network or out on the internet.</li>
					<li><b>Probe groups</b>: several instances per location share the monitors. If one stops, the others take over within a minute.</li>
					<li><b>Test</b> runs an unsaved monitor from every location in seconds, with a timing waterfall from DNS to transfer.</li>
					<li><b>Folders and dependencies</b>: while a parent is down its children show Impacted and their alerts stay quiet, so an outage pages once.</li>
					<li><b>Alerts per monitor</b> through the shared channels: down, degraded, or a certificate about to expire.</li>
					<li><b>YAML import and export</b> with a preview, for reviewing monitors in git.</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="lede" style="font-size:0.95rem">Synthetics runs on a control plane. Results land in a Site project as ordinary metrics, so dashboards and PromQL work on them too.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="specimen">
				<div class="lbl">Monitors · 3 locations</div>
				<div class="mini">
					<div class="folder">Payments/EU</div>
