				<h2>Every asset, its health and the reason</h2>
				<ul>
					<li><b>One inventory</b> of clusters, nodes, hosts, namespaces, workloads, pods, containers and services, built every 5 minutes from data your agents already send.</li>
					<li><b>Health with the reason</b>: CPU, memory, disk, restarts, replicas, error logs and firing alerts.</li>
					<li><b>Lifecycle and a change feed</b>: new, not reporting, terminated, restarted.</li>
					<li><b>Tree or table</b>, with charts per asset and links straight into its logs, traces and dashboards.</li>
					<li><b>Cloud connections</b> add what runs no agent: load balancers, databases, buckets, functions and scaling groups from AWS accounts and Azure subscriptions. VMs and clusters join the hosts and clusters your agents report.</li>
					<li><b>Read-only, keyless</b>: a wizard writes the CloudFormation, Bicep or CLI. A probe group scans with its own identity, a role, or a federated token. Obzly stores identifiers only.</li>
					<li><b>Cloud health</b>: a full discovery every 4 hours and a health scan of what it found every 15 minutes: instance status checks, load balancer targets and Azure Resource Health.</li>
